{
  "case_id": "2017-17-387",
  "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DAVID S. HAWKINS, ESQ., Sedro-Woolley, Washington; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nANN O'CONNELL, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, in support of the Petitioner.\nERIC D. MILLER, ESQ., Seattle, Washington; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Upper Skagit Indian Tribe",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Respondents sued the tribe to challenge the tribe's title of record to the property at issue. This Court has consistently held that sovereign immunity bars suits against tribal governments. Respondents' own prayer for relief establishes that their suit is an attack on the tribe's interests in the property, confirming that sovereign immunity bars their claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. O'Connell: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nI'd like to start with Justice Kagan's questions about what is the baseline here about what sovereign immunity entails. The baseline is sovereign immunity from suit. This is the Alexander Hamilton quote from the Federalist Papers: \"It is inherent in the nature of sovereignty not to be amenable\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, you say it's been made -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, of course, this Court said in the Permanent Mission of India case that the Foreign Sovereign Immunities Act was meant \"to codify the preexisting real property exception to sovereign immunity recognized by international practice.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. O'CONNELL",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. O'CONNELL: Well, I -- I think that's because it is -- it is up to Congress -\u00ad this Court has consistently said it's up to Congress to control and make exceptions to the immunity from suit of Indian tribes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But I thought that we explained in Kiowa that foreign sovereign immunity actually started as a judicial doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Ms. O'Connell,one -- there was one sentence in your brief that really leapt off the page, for me anyway. It's the one between pages 23 and 24 where you say the Respondents, the Lundgrens, you're asking, well, what alternatives do they have? And you say the Lundgrens could, for example, log trees on the disputed strip, commence building a structure, or take other similar actions that would induce Petitioner to file suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT ON BEHALF OF ERIC D. MILLER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought that the -\u00ad that Justice Ginsburg's question which started off this line of questioning was essentially this: Suppose there were no such thing as the immovable property exception. It just doesn't exist or doesn't apply in this situation. Would the decision of the Washington Supreme Court be correct based on the in rem theory?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there were -- I mean, no, it would not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but you -\u00ad that's not quite right, though, because we know the United States would be immune from this suit, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the land were in trust, the sovereign immunity of the United States would bar the suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government raised the immovable property argument in its brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We had a conversation with the Solicitor General."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Look, sending it back -- sending it back, I think it is a -- we could try to decide it or we could say: Review, not first view, all right? So one of the things -\u00ad ways in my mind is this, that reading the words \"immunity from suit\" broadly, extending where not even Canada would dare to go, all right, there's a lot of language in cases that does say that. So I'm pretty curious, whether anyone else is, but I'm pretty curious, for the last 20 years, how have things gone?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "a state's jurisdiction to control the ownership and disposition of real property within its territory is a core sovereign prerogative."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the record show -- this parcel of land is about an acre, is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2017-17-387",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bcac7070eab16f0879fb1a5f8b8c6466b5006886a104699371b4f53549b05789",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bcac7070eab1-0002-0010",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's correct, Your Honor."
    },
